WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.940
- This video was made
possible by Tab for a Cause.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.840
If you are a subscriber to this channel,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.170
you are a Legal Eagle,
that means you want to know

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.950
how the laws that govern our
everyday lives actually work.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.740
You know that the world is complicated

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.880
and you're not willing to
settle for the easy answers

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.980
that pundits love to provide.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.840
You believe that understanding
the law is crucial

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.700
to being an informed citizen

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.940
and you are not willing to turn away,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.370
even when you get answers
that you don't like.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.490
You're here to think like a lawyer.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.674
So, my fellow Legal Eagles,
in 2019, I say to you,

00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:36.663
(fireworks blasting)
caw-caw.

00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:37.531
(eagle screeching)

00:00:37.531 --> 00:00:40.010
And if you're looking for
more killer legal analysis,

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.150
I thought it might be
helpful to make a list

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.530
of the five best attorneys
to follow in 2019.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.990
Fair warning, this list is
gonna be pretty politics-heavy,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.380
because I think that those are some

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.880
of the most important
legal issues of the day,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.040
maybe that will change in 2020,
but that's where we are now.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.010
So let' start out with
an honorable mention,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.870
who is not actually a lawyer,
but who's legal analysis

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.690
is so good that I almost
included him on this list

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.520
and that's Ben Wittes of the Lawfare blog.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.590
He's not a lawyer,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.420
he's a little bit on
the conservative side,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.210
but in my view, nobody knows more

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.120
about National Security
law on the internet today.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.050
And as Mr Wittes likes to point out,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.700
democratic norms are being
broken all over the place

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.120
in this current world that we live in,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.570
but it's bringing people together

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.670
from all over the political spectrum.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.650
I share Mr Wittes' request
that when this is all over,

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.070
everyone remember the
shared democratic principles

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.130
that brought us together
in these trying times.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.780
So definitely check out Ben Wittes

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.610
and the entire Lawfare blog

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.220
and podcast community, they are great.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.730
(heavy rock music)

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.390
So that brings us to fifth place

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.150
for the top lawyers to follow in 2019

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.340
and that goes to Leonard French.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.480
Moving away from politics for the moment,

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.860
as your second favorite
Copyright Attorney,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.610
I can highly recommend your first favorite

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.580
Copyright Attorney, Leonard French.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.180
Leonard French is a Copyright
Attorney and YouTuber

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.150
known for wearing funny hats,

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.560
while he gives great legal analysis,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.760
he tends to livestream
before he goes to work,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.230
so you can catch him early in
the mornings or late at night,

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.430
he often goes straight
into the legal briefs

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.320
of famous copyright cases

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.070
or other legal cases of
the day and it's great,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.820
because you rarely get a chance
to see the actual language

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.770
and paperwork that gets
filed in these things

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.680
and he provides great analysis.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.360
His YouTube channel, the Lawful
Masses with Leonard French

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.090
is great for copyright news of the day,

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.090
especially for video game related news,

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.740
it's a little wonky, but
that's how we like it here.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.430
(heavy rock music)

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.200
So that takes us to fourth place

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.090
and that goes to Seth Abramson.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.240
He is a former state and
federal public defender,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.450
there's going to be a lot
of Assistant US Attorneys

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.040
and District Attorneys on this list,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.020
so it's nice to get the
perspective of a public defender.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.950
Currently Seth Abramson focuses
on the Trump Administration

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.490
and all of the legal issues

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.600
that the administration is facing.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.240
He gets a lot of flack for
not doing original reporting

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.410
and for being extremely
long-winded, like Twitter threads

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.170
that are hundreds of posts
long, and fair enough,

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.170
but for my money, no one is examining

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.660
the publicly available evidence

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.260
in more detail than Seth Abramson.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.560
Note however, that he tends
to be extremely partisan,

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.930
so I would take all of his
analysis with a grain of salt,

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.760
maybe dial it back 25 or 30%, but still,

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.760
when news cycles don't even last 24 hours,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.650
we need someone to be able to cull through

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.230
the deluge of news that
we're getting everyday

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.510
and look at things from
a lawyer's perspective

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.910
and a lot of the analysis

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.910
that Seth Abramson is
doing is really top-notch.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.390
(heavy rock music)

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.200
All right, so that takes us to third place

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.790
and that goes to two lawyers,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.310
Renato Mariotti and Asha Rangappa,

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:44.550
who are often hosts of
the On Topic podcast.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.780
I mention both, because while the podcast

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.220
is Renato Mariotti's, he
often has Asha Rangappa on,

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.290
and frankly, the podcast is never better,

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.760
than when she provides
her analysis as well.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.120
Both are former Assistant US Attorneys,

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.780
which essentially is
like a District Attorney,

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.500
but for the Federal government.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.310
Renato worked on the civil side,

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.960
while Asha worked on the
counter-intelligence side,

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.420
so they're analysis together
is especially invaluable.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.560
You can also find both of them on Twitter,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.980
but they're also not afraid
to do an emergency podcast

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.730
to stay on top of this news cycle,

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.430
that is burying people in
new things every single day,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.325
so definitely check out
the On Topic podcast.

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:22.770
(heavy rock music)

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.430
So that takes us to second place

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.750
and that easily goes to Preet Bharara,

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.010
who is the host of the Stay Tuned podcast

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.941
and tweets @PreetBharara.

00:04:30.941 --> 00:04:32.010
Preet Bharara was in charge

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.870
of the Southern District of New York,

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.370
which is often considered

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.050
one of the most prestigious
Federal District courts.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.930
Not only does the Southern
District of New York

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.210
tend to handle a lot of
high-profile terrorists

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.820
and related cases, because of
the fact that New York City

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.400
is in the Southern District of New York,

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.730
they also tend to handle almost all

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:51.430
of the very high-profile financial crimes

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.250
by virtue of Wall Street being
in the Southern District.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.420
Note that he was a democratic appointee

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.710
who was personally fired by the President,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.350
so you'll probably need
to take his analysis

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.430
with a grain of salt,
but I think he is one

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.340
of the best interviewers
on the planet right now,

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.586
you cannot miss his podcast.

00:05:06.586 --> 00:05:09.060
(heavy rock music)

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.240
So that takes us to number one

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.900
and that goes to Ken
White, who tweets @Popehat

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.350
and is in charge of All
the President's Lawyers

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.130
and the First Amendment
podcast, Make No Law,

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.390
Ken White is a former

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.710
Assistant US Attorney
turned Defense Attorney,

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.370
who's also done a fair amount
of First Amendment law.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.360
He also has a very skeptical view

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.060
of government and prosecutorial
power, which I find,

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.080
makes his analysis both
accurate and hilarious.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.440
It's hard to describe just how good

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.190
Ken White's Twitter account is.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.550
It is, I think, by far, the
best thing on Twitter right now,

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.950
so if you're not following
@Popehat on Twitter,

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.790
stop everything that you're
doing and subscribe now.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.040
Sometimes it's hard to follow him,

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.930
because his handle's always
some variation of hat,

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.450
so at the time of this
video, it's Hamberder Hat,

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.710
which relates to a President's tweet.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:59.330
In the past it's been Covfefe
Hat, VeryLegalVeryCool Hat,

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.310
his podcast, All the President's Lawyers,

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:05.340
in addition to having the
greatest name for a podcast,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.750
is fantastic, it's hosted
by journalist Josh Barrow,

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.130
who does a great job
playing the straight man

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:13.660
to Ken White's legal analysis
and breaking things down

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.260
from a layman's perspective.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.040
When I do a podcast, I'm
gonna try and make it

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.970
half as good as All the
President's Lawyers.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.400
Ken White is known for taking

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.310
a very dim view of the RICO statutes,

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:27.230
please tell him to make
a It's not RICO t-shirt,

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:30.520
because it's not RICO, it's never RICO,

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.770
but maybe this time.
(fireworks blasting)

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.750
Caw-caw.
(eagle screeching)

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.260
So go and check out those lawyers

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.430
and while you're browsing the net,

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.660
you can raise money for charity,
just by opening new tabs,

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.600
which you were going to do anyway.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.540
Tab for a Cause is a
Google Chrome extension

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.570
that allows you to pick
a charity of your choice

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.980
and then every time you open up a new tab,

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.250
instead of it being blank,
it displays a couple of ads

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.900
and the money that you generate
is donated to your charity,

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.100
there is no charge to you

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.100
and it does some good for the world.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.510
Tab for a Cause users have raised

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:02.140
hundreds of thousands
of dollars for charity,

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:05.070
it is the easiest possible
way to donate to charity,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.610
so just click on the
link in the description

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.390
and download the extension
and do some good,

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.630
by doing what you were going to do anyway.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:12.760
So did I get that right?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.230
Are there other lawyers that you follow

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:16.800
that you think I should
also follow in 2019?

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.523
Let me know and until next
time, I'll see you in court.

